<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>A vector with a given magnitude</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Give a vector with magnitude \({@M@}\) that is neither horizontal nor vertical (both components non-zero). (There are many correct answers.)</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>You need \(x^2 + y^2 = {@M@}^2 = {@M^2@}\) with \(x\) and \(y\) both non-zero: look for two square numbers that add up to \({@M^2@}\).</p><p>\({@ex[1]^2@} + {@ex[2]^2@} = {@M^2@}\), so \({@ta@}\) works, and so do \({@col(ex)@}\), \({@col(reverse(ex))@}\) and any of these with signs changed.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
col(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]]);
/* Design: give a vector with a given magnitude, graded by property: any vector with magnitude M and two non-zero components scores. Only 6 values of M, so variants come from M and the sign pattern of the teacher's answer (24 notes). Source: original. */
ml: [[5,[3,4]],[10,[6,8]],[13,[5,12]],[20,[12,16]],[17,[8,15]],[25,[7,24]]];
j: 1+rand(6); M: ml[j][1]; ex: ml[j][2];
sg: rand([[1,1],[1,-1],[-1,1],[-1,-1]]);
ta: col([sg[1]*ex[1], sg[2]*ex[2]]);
tr: col([sg[1]*ex[2], sg[2]*ex[1]]);
tax: matrix([M],[0]); t4: matrix([1],[M-1]); t5: matrix([1],[1]);
/* decimal test inputs (fairness) */
ftax: float(tax); fdec: float(matrix([3*M/5],[-4*M/5]));
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>M={@M@}, signs {@sg@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Vectors: a vector with a given magnitude</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 2.2: Construct a vector with a given whole-number magnitude and two non-zero components.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question 7 in Exercise B of Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 4 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: any vector of the magnitude rather than one parallel to a given vector, new magnitudes, STACK randomisation, with named feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
